  {
    "id": "026e3ae1-ad0a-457c-b8f8-88b972bd62f5",
    "question": "Was the earlier 'Poll Management: Not found' finding accurate?",
    "answer": "No — corrected 2026-08-31. Before building a new poll feature (recommended as 'cleanest gap to close' in an earlier doc), did a live verification pass and found Poll Management already fully real in sohamyoga-frontend: poll/poll_option/poll_vote tables (tenant-scoped, DB-level duplicate-vote prevention via UNIQUE constraint), confirmed live in Postgres (real table, 0 rows), /api/community/polls with real SQL joins and vote counting, /admin/polls and /community/polls UI both fetching the real API with zero MOCK_* constants. The original miss: earlier audits scoped 'poll management' checks to market-research-portal only and never checked the sibling sohamyoga-frontend app, where it turned out to live. Corrected both docs/advanced-management-feature-list-gap-analysis.md and docs/chatgpt-extracts/twenty-five-item-advanced-management-list.md in place rather than leaving the stale claim. Lesson: when a gap-check spans a multi-app repo, must explicitly check both apps before concluding 'not found', not just the app currently in focus.",
