  {
    "id": "15f68000-219b-4518-87c5-01ba9b1bb56c",
    "question": "What replaced the fake *.ab_testing FeatureFlag entries?",
    "answer": "Built a real Experimentation/A-B-testing framework in sohamyoga-frontend to close the confirmed gap from the 25-item management-list audit (only fake on/off FeatureFlag entries named *.ab_testing existed, referencing GrowthBook/PostHog as an undelivered promise, zero real variant assignment or lift measurement). New: src/domain/experimentation/db-schema.sql (experiment/experiment_variant/experiment_assignment, tenant-scoped, applied live to Postgres), Experiment.ts (deterministic SHA-256 sticky bucketing, real two-proportion z-test with an honest 30-sample-per-variant floor before reporting significance), /api/experiments (admin CRUD: create/add_variant/start/stop, server-enforced guardrails — rejects starting without allocations summing to exactly 100% or without a marked control), /api/experiments/[key]/assign (public, unauthenticated, sticky assignment keyed to the same anonymous_id/user_id tracking_event already uses), and /admin/experiments (full 8-tab Operational Portal Page & Tab Standard, added to admin nav). Verified live end-to-end: created an experiment, confirmed 409 on starting with 0 variants and on over-100% allocation, started successfully at exactly 100%, assigned 10 distinct subjects via the public endpoint and confirmed sticky re-assignment, inserted one real tracking_event conversion and confirmed the GET stats route correctly joined it to the right variant via a live SQL join (no fabricated lift). Confirmed all 8 tabs render on the live hydrated page via a headless-browser check (curl alone showed a loading gate, so used Playwright). Noted but did not fix: a pre-existing, unrelated duplicate React key warning from two identical '/admin/videos' nav entries in admin/layout.tsx (lines 76 and 260) — out of scope for this task. tsc --noEmit clean (only 3 pre-existing, unrelated ClassSequence.test.ts errors remain). All test data cleaned up.",
