  {
    "id": "0c24021b-9c60-4bab-97ec-cb40ecdc4f46",
    "question": "How was the 'I still don't have clarity on what's built vs missing' feedback addressed?",
    "answer": "Saved a new mandatory global policy (policy_module_understanding_standard.md, referenced in ~/.claude/CLAUDE.md) requiring every module to have user/admin/data flow, job, report, dashboard, schema, flowchart, user story, I/P/O, final outcome, and built-vs-missing documented in one place — never scattered chat answers. Built the real backing: module_registry table (sohamyoga-frontend, app-scoped so it covers both apps), populated honestly in two tiers — 6 modules (Voice AI, Poll Management, Experiments, Hooks, CRM/Leads, Operations & Failure Tracking) with FULL verified detail from this session's actual builds, plus 18 summary rows from the 25-item management-list audit with real built_status + citations but explicitly flagged 'flow/schema detail not yet cataloged' rather than fabricated. Built /api/admin/module-registry (GET with live tally + an honest denominator: 24 cataloged vs an estimated 61 real admin-nav surfaces in sohamyoga-frontend alone, counted by parsing admin/layout.tsx, not guessed) and /admin/module-registry UI (filterable by app/status, full per-module detail panel). Added a real monitoring job (ModuleRegistryDriftSweepJob, daily 05:30 UTC, registered in CronRegistry+jobModules) that flags stale (>30d unverified) or incomplete (claimed real/partial but missing user_flow/admin_flow) registry rows — verified live via the real on-demand job runner, confirmed a real operation_run row with status=succeeded. Verified the full UI live via headless browser (login, API tally, page render, click-through detail panel showing real schema tables and job name). Explicitly did NOT fabricate flow/schema detail for the ~37 remaining uncataloged admin surfaces — they show as 'not yet cataloged', which is itself the honest answer to 'what's still missing.' Not yet built (deferred, communicated to user): Kaggle/synthetic tagged test-data generation for end-to-end module testing — flagged as next-phase work, not attempted this pass.",
