  {
    "id": "d5096e45-5473-4f04-b150-92f2903f6174",
    "question": "What did the second module-cataloging batch (Booking, Wellness, E-commerce) find?",
    "answer": "Real code/schema audit, no guessing: Booking (partial) — admin-side Overview/Today/Upcoming/Waitlist/No-shows/Rules/Reports is real and API-backed, but /booking and /booking/[classId] are pure mock UI with a fake setTimeout 'booking' — grep-confirmed zero INSERT INTO booking anywhere, so no customer can actually book a class end-to-end. Wellness (not_built) — health_profile/body_metrics/daily_wellness_log/wearable_sync tables have zero API routes at all; /admin/wellness is 100% mock (source literally commented '// Mock data'); the real wellness-scoring cron job doesn't even touch this schema, it scores a different domain (student.practice_journal) which is itself never populated by any app code either — a real job with no live input. E-commerce (partial) — admin product/vendor/inventory CRUD and the abandoned-cart-recovery job are real and DB-backed, but no storefront/checkout exists (/catalog is an unrelated hardcoded yoga-class list) and grep confirms zero INSERT INTO sales_order anywhere, so the abandoned-cart job has no live input in practice. All 3 added to module_registry with full detail (docs/domain/module-registry/seed-2026-08-31-batch2.sql). Registry now covers 27 modules (16 real, 9 partial, 2 not_built) of an estimated 61 sohamyoga-frontend admin surfaces. Verified live via API.",
