  {
    "id": "d81daf0a-3f10-490b-89fb-89e8a9f56558",
    "question": "What was built to fix the real Booking gap found in the module audit?",
    "answer": "Wired the actual booking-creation path that was previously entirely mock (grep-confirmed zero INSERT INTO booking anywhere before this). Added level/style/price columns to class_session (real extension the mock UI already implied but the schema never had). Seeded 4 real near-future class sessions (one deliberately capacity=2 to exercise the waitlist path). Built GET /api/classes (public, live spotsLeft computed from real bookings), GET /api/classes/[id], and POST /api/bookings (customer-authenticated, resolves student_id from student.user_id, row-locks class_session via a real transaction to prevent overbooking races, inserts a confirmed booking or falls back to a real waitlist_entry with correct position, rejects duplicate bookings with a clear 409). Rewired /booking and /booking/[classId] off their hardcoded CLASS_DATA/setTimeout mock onto these real APIs, with real error and waitlisted states surfaced to the customer. Verified live end-to-end as a real logged-in customer: confirmed booking succeeded, duplicate booking correctly rejected (409), filled a 2-capacity class and confirmed the 3rd booking correctly waitlisted (position 1), confirmed spotsLeft recalculated correctly after each, confirmed the real /booking page renders live class data with correct Book Now / Full states via headless browser. Found and fixed a real bug during this verification: the DATE column came back as a JS Date object from pg, producing a malformed dateTime string (e.g. 'Tue Sep 01 2026...T07:00:00') until formatted properly. All test student/booking/waitlist rows cleaned up afterward; the 4 real class_session rows were left as legitimate seed data. Updated the module_registry row for 'booking' from partial to real, with an honest remaining-gap note (no payment gateway, no customer-side cancellation, no auto waitlist-promotion job).",
