  {
    "id": "dd8eec73-df66-495b-8b5d-fe095b7e1b15",
    "question": "Deep re-audit of Ads Management + 8 platform/comms modules: what changed?",
    "answer": "Applied the same skepticism that caught Booking/E-commerce's fake creation flows to Ads Management and found the same pattern: real schema + real reporting, but zero code path to create/launch a campaign (2 INSERT INTO ad_campaign hits total: a demo seeder and a health-audit job that never touches campaigns), zero real ad-platform API clients, and dead onClick-less 'New Campaign'/'AI Generate Ad' buttons. Extended the audit to 8 more modules and found ONE shared root cause explains most of them: PostizSocialAutoPublishJob.ts and NotificationDispatchJob.ts are both real, correct HTTP client code (POST to self-hosted Postiz/Novu instances) but neither backend is deployed in this repo and neither API key is set — so YouTube/Facebook/LinkedIn organic posting and email dispatch are all 'partial: real code, credential-gated, not mocked' rather than N separate problems. Telegram is a special case: a real, unit-tested bot-send function with zero production callers anywhere. Google Business Reviews is the one genuine surprise — fully real end-to-end with actual OAuth + real Google API calls, upgraded to full registry detail. Google Ads (the specific platform, distinct from generic ad_campaign schema) is confirmed not_built — zero client code, one disabled feature flag whose own description says it needs a developer token. CORRECTED two of my own earlier WRONG registry classifications from shallow checks: paid-ads and campaign-management were marked 'real' based on 'admin page exists'; deep audit found campaign launch is a pure UPDATE lifecycle_campaign SET status= with zero send-side-effect (identical dead-CTA pattern to Ads). Registry now at 32 modules (14 real, 15 partial, 3 not_built) — the partial count grew mainly from correcting over-generous earlier claims, which is the intended function of this registry, not a regression.",
