  {
    "id": "879818b8-d011-4797-9eb1-4fc86ba32465",
    "question": "Was a new BOT UI / RAG / job system built from scratch for the agent console?",
    "answer": "No — discovered and reused already-real, already-built infrastructure instead of duplicating it (per user_working_style memory: 'agentic-ollama-platform has plan/schedule/execute/monitor/fallback, don't rebuild it'). Found sohamyoga-frontend already had a complete server-side bridge (src/lib/agent.ts: submitGoal/requestStatus/agentHealth, with circuit-breaker via operation-ledger) and API routes (/api/ai/agent, /api/ai/agent/[id]) wired to the agentic-ollama-platform gateway (port 8091, FastAPI, real planner -> task queue -> workers) — but the gateway process wasn't running and no UI page exposed it. Started the real gateway (serve.sh), verified /health returns real {ollama:true,service:up}, then built the one missing piece: /admin/agent-console, a real 'BOT UI' where an admin types a goal and it's genuinely planned by Ollama into tasks and executed by real workers. Verified live end-to-end via headless browser: submitted 'Say hello in one short sentence', watched real task decomposition appear (Retrieve greeting phrase template -> Fill in template), confirmed via network log that GET/POST /api/ai/agent and repeated polling GET /api/ai/agent/[id] all returned real 200/202 responses — genuine planning latency (~8-15s for Ollama to plan) caused two early false-negative test checks before the real behavior was confirmed with a longer wait. Also updated policy_module_understanding_standard.md with 3 new mandatory sections requested this turn: per-dimension tallies (User Flow UI / Admin UI / DB / Report / Dashboard counts), the 3-required-execution-paths rule (BOT/Manual/Pipeline, each verified independently), and RAG-backed data extraction for draft documentation + synthetic test data (grounded, never hallucinated, human-reviewed before being marked verified). Real Playwright e2e re-run also kicked off in background (was 7 days stale) — in progress, ~300+ tests through with some genuine NPS-related failures surfacing, not yet complete.",
