  {
    "id": "49c4baa7-0fab-41bd-80da-95c3e7e1f786",
    "question": "Consolidated status: what got built in the late-session burst while the user was away?",
    "answer": "Built and live-verified: (1) Module registry dimension tallies (userFlowUI/adminUI/database/report/dashboard counts) via explicit boolean columns rather than fragile text-pattern matching, exposed in /api/admin/module-registry and /admin/module-registry UI. (2) Real BOT UI at /admin/agent-console -- discovered and reused already-existing agentic-ollama-platform gateway (planner->queue->workers) plus already-coded but unwired bridge (src/lib/agent.ts, /api/ai/agent routes); started the real gateway process and built only the missing UI piece; verified live with a real submitted goal producing real Ollama-planned tasks. (3) Real service catalog (market-research-portal): service_catalog_item schema, /api/service-catalog, public /services page with category filter + inquiry modal reusing the existing real lead-capture path (extended with serviceItemId); verified live end-to-end including the resulting lead's FK link to the correct service. (4) Closed a previously-flagged adversarial-review gap while touching leads/capture: added rate limiting (5/min/IP) and email format validation, verified live (429 on 6th rapid request, 400 on malformed email). (5) Policy expanded with sections 6-9 (per-dimension tallies, 3 required execution paths [BOT/Manual/Pipeline], 'no demo counts as real without live proof' rule, RAG-backed drafting). Captured but NOT built, written into docs/session-plan-2026-08-31-customer-portal-and-bot-expansion.md rather than guessed at: real load testing for '1000 concurrent users' claim, Cal.com calendar integration, email campaign design/send (blocked same as before -- Novu undeployed), purchase/checkout/billing (blocked -- no payment gateway exists anywhere in either app, confirmed by grep). Real Playwright e2e re-run (was 7 days stale) ran in background through 500+ tests with some genuine failures surfacing (NPS boundary tests, several admin pages with real console errors) -- not yet fully complete/reported at time of this log.",
