  {
    "id": "40e6a33a-f7a7-461f-9e3d-74989db81c63",
    "question": "Real e2e re-run completed (was 7 days stale) — what did it find?",
    "answer": "466 passed / 59 failed out of 525 (88.8%), 32.8 min runtime, across 3 browser projects (chrome-desktop/mobile-pwa/color-blind-protanopia). Root-caused and fixed the single largest failure cluster: CONSOLE-001/002/003 tests failed identically across all 3 browsers on the exact same 6 admin pages (demo-hub, ai-governance, teachers, students, social/scheduler, simulation) plus 2 detail-page tests — traced to a duplicate '/admin/videos' entry in admin/layout.tsx's nav array (found earlier this session while building Experiments, not fixed until now) causing a real React 'duplicate key' console.error on every single admin page render. Removed the duplicate (kept the simpler 'Videos' label entry, removed the redundant 'Video & Reel Management' one), verified live via headless browser that all 6 previously-failing pages now show zero console errors. This one-line fix likely resolves ~18-27 of the 59 total failures (6-8 distinct test cases x 3 browsers). Remaining failure clusters NOT yet investigated: NPS-003/004/006 (boundary score 0/10 rejected, invitation token reuse, nps-records — failing identically across all 3 browsers, looks like a real regression not flakiness), MCPG-005 (staff_approval 403 check), TRACKING-003 (consent-gate bypass check), DEMO-005/SIM-002 (Demo Hub reports), SPE-002 (Postiz provider health), VIR-002/004 and MR-002 (browser-specific, only 1 of 3 browsers, more likely flaky). Did not fix the remaining ~40 failures this pass — surfaced honestly rather than guessed at, since root-causing each needs real investigation the same way the console-error cluster did.",
    "timestamp": "2026-08-31T06:47:57.272Z",
    "tags": [
      "bug-fix",
      "e2e",
      "governance",
      "react",
      "verification"
    ],
