  {
    "id": "6e9f53a7-9929-45f1-a58a-e06d684d6ec9",
    "question": "What was the real root cause of the NPS-003/004/006 e2e failures, and was it fixed?",
    "answer": "Two distinct real causes, both fixed and verified live (45/45 tests passing across all 3 browser projects after fix). (1) Stale test code: the post-class-experience survey now has consent_required=true (a real compliance feature added later than these tests), but 5 POST call sites in nps-feedback.spec.ts never sent consent:true, so the API was correctly rejecting them -- not an API bug, the tests were outdated. Fixed by adding consent:true to all 5 call sites (score-0 boundary, score-10 boundary, both requests in the token-reuse-409 test, the NPS-004 end-to-end test, and the NPS-006 nps-records test). (2) Separately, while investigating, hit a real 500 unrelated to my fix: 'Cannot find module ./vendor-chunks/@opentelemetry.js' -- the sohamyoga-frontend dev server had been running continuously since Aug26 (5+ days, spanning this entire marathon session's huge number of file changes) and its .next webpack cache was corrupted, same failure pattern as an earlier session note for market-research-portal. Killed the stale process, cleared .next/cache, restarted clean, confirmed http 200 and clean compile. This fixes the NPS cluster (18 of the original 59 e2e failures: 6 test cases x 3 browsers) for real, verified with actual live Playwright runs against the freshly-restarted server, not just code review.",
