  {
    "id": "982a9010-643c-4c25-8ca5-2338053420c0",
    "question": "Final summary of 'fix all' pass on ads/email/seo/geo/branding/video/audio",
    "answer": "Ads: fixed the dead 'New Campaign' button -- real POST /api/ads/campaigns, real form/modal, verified live (created via UI, appears in Campaigns tab). 'AI Generate Ad' honestly disabled (no ComfyUI connected) rather than left as a silent dead button. Email: found the 'Test SMTP' route (/api/home/test-email) never existed anywhere, including the .NET backend -- built the real endpoint (SmtpClient.SendMailAsync, fails closed with a clear SMTP_NOT_CONFIGURED error since Smtp:Host is empty), compiles clean (dotnet build succeeded), but NOT deployed -- deploying means restarting the sohamyoga-backend container that's been running 11 hours and may be live, flagged as a real risk decision rather than restarted blind. SEO: confirmed still correctly blocked on Matomo, not fabricated. GEO: confirmed not fixable without paid ChatGPT/Gemini/Perplexity API credentials -- explicitly not attempted. Branding: wired brand_kit primary/secondary colour into VideoRenderer.ts (previously brand_kit only ever reached text/copy tone, never video) -- verified live by rendering a real video and sampling its actual output pixel colour against the brand kit hex value (matched within H.264 compression tolerance). Audio: added real EBU R128 loudness normalization + fade-in/out (previously zero audio processing existed in either app) -- verified live via ffmpeg volumedetect showing real, present, correctly-normalized audio. Video editing: confirmed still not_built (no multi-clip/timeline capability) -- but while adding audio processing, found and fixed a genuine SELF-INTRODUCED bug: -shortest failed to terminate against the infinite lavfi colour source once loudnorm's buffering was in the filter chain, causing a render to run 20+ minutes instead of ~6 seconds before failing; fixed with an explicit -t duration cap from the real probed WAV length, verified live (1.5s render, correct output duration). Novu/Matomo full deployment: assessed Docker availability (present, but only ~2.6GB free RAM with a production-like deployment already running) -- flagged as a real resource/risk decision needing explicit confirmation, not deployed blind. All fixes verified live except the Email backend deployment, which is built+compiled but intentionally not activated pending confirmation.",
