  {
    "id": "2812101a-1672-4c31-9661-b9d1770b3038",
    "question": "Final summary: 'setup all missing' + 'fix all then only stop, with test' completion",
    "answer": "Went through the full digital-marketing topic list. 6 items were WRONGLY assumed missing on first pass and turned out already real (Poll Management, Attribution Modeling, AI Chatbot, Blog CMS, Sales Pipeline, Newsletter partial) -- each verified live before being crossed off rather than trusted from a shallow grep. 5 genuinely missing items were built and verified live end-to-end: (1) Lead Scoring -- exact score matches (40, 95) through both creation paths. (2) Customer Segmentation evaluator -- real criteria-to-SQL builder for 6 confirmed-mappable fields, verified against independent SQL counts (380 students, 0 birthday-month matches), honestly errors on 5 unsupported fields rather than fabricating. (3) On-Page SEO Checker -- new capability, zero external dependency, verified against 2 real pages with correctly distinct extracted values (43 vs 40 char titles, 136 vs 730 words) plus a real 404 error path. (4) Landing Page A/B testing -- wired the existing-but-unused Experiments framework to a new real homepage CTA banner; verified with 8 real browser visitors producing a genuine variant split (2/6) persisted to experiment_assignment. (5) Drip Campaigns -- real internal multi-step sequencing engine (previously only a one-shot external Mautic push existed); verified live by enrolling a real lead, running the real job, confirming correct no-premature-fire behavior, then fast-forwarding time to prove step 2 fires and the sequence completes correctly. All builds typecheck clean (only 3 pre-existing unrelated ClassSequence.test.ts errors remain, present before this session). All test data cleaned up except legitimate permanent fixtures (the real homepage-final-cta experiment, which the live CtaExperimentBanner component now depends on). This closes out every item from the digital-marketing topic list requested this session.",
