  {
    "id": "a909913f-ff46-44f2-8c75-070f58824a91",
    "question": "Was the admin panel's client-side auth actually working in a real browser, and was the Wellness module built?",
    "answer": "Built Health & Wellness admin (/admin/wellness): real health_profile/body_metrics/daily_wellness_log/wearable_sync CRUD (previously 100% mock), HIPAA/PIPEDA-compliant legal-basis gate + wellness_audit trail on profile access/delete, real analytics from the 3 pre-existing DB views. Found and fixed 2 real bugs: a Postgres param-type conflict blocking all wearable-status writes, and a wellness_audit FK with no ON DELETE action that blocked the admin_destructive delete_health_profile tool entirely (migration 129, ON DELETE SET NULL). SEPARATELY, and more significant: discovered the entire admin panel's client-side auth check (admin/layout.tsx calling authApi.getCurrentUser() cross-origin to the .NET backend at NEXT_PUBLIC_API_URL) has been silently broken in real browsers all session -- the backend's Cors:AllowedOrigins allowlist (SohamYoga.Web/appsettings.json) only ever listed localhost:3000/3001, never updated when this session moved the frontend dev port to 8095, so every admin page's auth check failed with a CORS error and silently bounced to the login screen. curl-based verification never caught this because curl does not enforce CORS. Fixed by adding http://127.0.0.1:8095 and http://localhost:8095 to the allowlist and restarting the backend (pid replaced, dotnet run --urls http://127.0.0.1:15070). Verified live: ai-governance.spec.ts GOV-003 (previously failing 3/3) and a new wellness page browser check both pass with zero console errors after the fix. Also fixed an unrelated real bug found investigating this: customer-self-service.spec.ts's top-level afterAll unconditionally deleted the shared customer_demo fixture every run, contradicting its own header comment about the fixture being shared/persistent -- removed the delete.",
