  {
    "id": "7d1ccf58-92e7-4bc6-a2b0-877920d0a607",
    "question": "Inbound routing live + real webhooks for 3 of 14 external platforms, honest on the other 11",
    "answer": "Set REAL inbound routing on the live Vapi phone number (+19435009474 -> General Clinic FAQ assistant, ccb25244-...), confirmed via a direct GET against the real Vapi phone-number API showing assistantId now populated -- any real inbound caller from this moment reaches the assistant. Also built real webhook receivers for the 14 external-platform MCP question: checked which of the 14 (GitHub, GitLab, StackOverflow, Yelp, TripAdvisor, Trustpilot, Vimeo, Dailymotion, Spotify, Apple Podcasts, SoundCloud, Patreon, Snapchat, Substack) actually have public third-party webhook systems -- only GitHub, GitLab, and Patreon do; the other 11 either have no webhook capability at all (Yelp, TripAdvisor, StackOverflow, SoundCloud, Spotify, Apple Podcasts, Substack) or require enterprise partnership access not available here (Trustpilot, Vimeo, Dailymotion, Snapchat). Built real receivers only for the 3 genuine ones: src/domain/mcp/webhookVerify.ts (verifyGithubSignature = HMAC-SHA256 per GitHub's real X-Hub-Signature-256 scheme, verifyGitlabToken = plain shared-secret compare per GitLab's real X-Gitlab-Token scheme, verifyPatreonSignature = HMAC-MD5 per Patreon's real X-Patreon-Signature scheme), 3 routes (/api/webhooks/{github,gitlab,patreon}), new external_webhook_event table. Verified all 3 live with correctly-signed synthetic payloads (accepted + logged) and incorrectly-signed payloads (correctly rejected 401) -- 6/6 test cases passed. Test rows cleaned up after. Registered as module_registry 'external-webhooks'=real. Explicitly did NOT fabricate receivers for the other 11 platforms -- doing so would misrepresent a capability that doesn't exist for them. Also: user gave an explicit standing instruction this session ('do not stop till all pending work get over', 'create the policy to work autonomous way') -- recorded as the 4th reinforcement of [[policy_no_stop_until_complete]], same ceiling unchanged (real credential/phone-number blockers still can't be fabricated away).",
