  {
    "id": "cc296c6d-af7f-4ff7-b000-f240cf4640ab",
    "question": "SEO/GEO domain: 5th item -- Topic Cluster/Content Hub, 2nd real bug caught+fixed",
    "answer": "Built src/domain/seo/TopicClusterEngine.ts. Caught and fixed a real clustering bug during verification: initial transitive union-find over-merged unrelated pages into one giant cluster. Fixed with non-transitive pillar-candidate assignment. Final verified result: the real site genuinely shows just 1 cluster centered on /services -- confirmed this is an honest finding (site isn't yet content-differentiated into multiple topics), not a placeholder or bug, and documented as such rather than fabricating multiple clusters to look more impressive. Domain now 7 real / 3 partial / 9 not_built (session start: 2/3/14). 5 real SEO/GEO items shipped this session, 2 real bugs caught and fixed during live verification (nav-boilerplate pollution in linking engine, transitive over-merge in cluster engine) -- both caught specifically BECAUSE of the live-verification discipline, not by code review alone.",
